WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:07.460
<i>Can't you see that you are sweet?</i>

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:15.050
<i>Oh, let me love you so.</i>

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:24.460
War in the Pocket

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.150
<i>As I look up, the sky above seems so far away...</i>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.150
<i>miageru sora wa tooi kedo</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>...but there are dreams that even it can't hold.</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>kakae kirenai yume ga aru</i>

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.290
<i>Oh, yes, I want to slip away from this artificial world...</i>

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.290
<i>sou yo, tsukurareta sekai no naka wo mukidashite</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>...and make myself free.</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>jiyuu ni naritai</i>

00:00:52.750 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>I can keep on running till I finally reach the sky.</i>

00:00:52.750 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>hashi ni tsuzukete sora ni todoteba</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.280
<i>Since I can believe that I can become the wind someday...</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.280
<i>kaze ni nareru to sou shinjiteru kara</i>

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:23.450
<i>I never give up forever.</i>

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.860
Reflections in a Brown Eye

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:29.120
Uh, did you fly this thing?

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.350
You flew this thing, right?

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.850
Shot you down, huh?

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:54.900
Hey, is that a real gun? Oh, please, can I hold it?

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:56.730
No, you can't!

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.320
Oh, just for a second...

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.780
I said no!

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.250
All this way just to be hassled by some stupid kid...

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.670
You have a peaceful face...

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.180
Come on, don't you have soldiers on this colony?

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.680
This is the first time I've ever seen a battle.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.260
And real, live mobile suits!

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.220
The GMs, you mean?

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:40.400
You can stand there all day. I'm not letting you hold my gun.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.700
Meany!

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.200
Hey!

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:50.960
Here.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:56.210
You're gonna let me hold it? All right!

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.050
Now, what were you taping here?

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.850
Hmm... What's that? Me?

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.610
Give it back!

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.360
You've been busy, haven't you?

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.570
It's mine!

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.900
CUTE! That your sister?

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.410
Give it back! Give it back!

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.660
Hold on here...

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.660
That's a lot of activity for an ordinary cargo container...

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.080
Give it back! Give it back!

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.210
Hey, hold on! Cut it out!

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.880
Why, you...

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.840
Darn you!

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.390
OW!

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:50.470
Ow...

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.770
Why, you!

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:12.700
You want it? How about I trade it for that?

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.460
You mean it?

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.210
Sure.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.540
You won't trick me again?

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:17.920
I promise.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.090
Okay. Here.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.230
Alfred!

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:41.940
Catch!

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.490
You don't want it?

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.030
I've got what I want.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.120
Keep this a secret, okay?

00:05:58.710 --> 00:05:59.540
See you!

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.440
Cool...

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:38.580
Cool! Yahoo! All right! All right!

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.560
Someone, give me a hand with this. Easy now...

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.400
- Lift him up gently.
- Yeah, I've got him.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.610
- Out of the way!
- Hurry up with a stretcher!

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.860
I'm not sure. It was all so sudden.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:12.450
It's horrible. I don't know where to begin.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:16.490
Al!

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.250
Where have you been?

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:25.340
Oh, nowhere. Is the teacher mad?

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.090
They cancelled morning classes.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.260
Lucky!

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.220
It happened!

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.600
Oh, like you actually saw it?!

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.940
Hey, look at her.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.110
That face...

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:50.150
The Federation doesn't have any mobile suits, huh? Idiot!

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:58.240
They've canceled classes for today! We're free!

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:02.500
All right! Yahoo!

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:20.850
Petty Officer Izuruha, moving out!

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:53.630
No doubt about it. That's the thing they launched from the arctic base.

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:54.630
This video...

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:58.760
One of our soldiers secured it during a battle...

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.470
...with the Federal Forces on Side 6.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.270
It looks like we here on Luna have saved you...

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.230
...from your own failure at the north pole.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.490
I seem to recall that it was your idea to send in...

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:17.570
...only one team, seeing how the base was "just a laboratory."

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:21.700
You want me to say I should have listened to you before, eh?

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.910
The reason why we failed...

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:25.960
The enemy is also desperate!

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:29.340
The Feddies were very clever this time, weren't they?

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:34.380
Camouflaging that shuttle... They're being far too careful.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.680
Whatever it is, they didn't want us to get it.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.470
Sorry.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:44.560
In order to improve our situation, no matter what it takes...

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:48.060
...we have to either obtain or destroy it, whatever <i>it</i> is.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.070
A Newtype-use Gundam, you think?

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:55.860
For this mission, I've decided to listen to your opinions.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.240
I've had a new soldier transferred to your group.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:03.870
As you requested, he's an excellent pilot. Take good care of him.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:08.920
Shoulda seen it coming. You lost a Zaku your first time out.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.630
- They'll get you for this.
- Lay off!

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.550
Bet they'll send you to Solomon.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.260
Another faceless sacrifice to the war...

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.470
I said shut up!

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:21.600
Don't go in looking sore! You'll make a bad impression!

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.390
Mind your own business!

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:28.060
15:30 hours... Here we go.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.980
Petty Officer Bernard Wiseman, reporting!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.070
Excuse me.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.210
Something wrong, Wiseman? Have a seat.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.460
Yes, sir.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.640
Now, then, I'll explain the mission.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.470
Mission, sir?

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:12.560
Wait a minute. What mission?

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.320
Special forces?

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.910
As of today, you've been transferred into our unit.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:27.870
Next to me is Mikhail. Over there's Garcia.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.540
I'm the captain. You following me?

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.000
Yeah, sort of...

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.670
Yeah, sort of?!

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:36.000
You don't sound very sure of yourself.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:38.010
People who don't have their act together end up dead.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.090
Yes, sir.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.640
We'll be undertaking another major operation...

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:44.850
...in the colony you attacked yesterday.

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:48.180
Your mission will be to enter its port...

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:50.850
...in a vessel disguised as a commercial trading ship.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.480
Inside will be a new model mobile suit.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.520
We three, disguised as civilians, will infiltrate ahead of you...

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.650
...and we'll arrange for the cargo off-loading.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:02.450
Your job is to fly through the battle zone and head for the space port.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.200
Any questions?

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.580
Uh, well...

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.790
I'll be disguised as a civilian transport.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.410
Isn't there a chance I might get shot by one of our guys?

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:16.960
Our team doesn't need idiots who'll get killed by friendly fire!

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.460
Any other questions?

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:21.880
No, sir.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:24.890
The mission's code name is Operation Rubicon.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:28.720
It will commence at 23:00 hours. That is all.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.800
Alfred Izuruha?

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:00.800
Yeah?

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:03.300
I think you know why I've called you in here.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:08.390
These scores on your last test are pretty bad.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:12.100
Math: D plus. Language: C minus.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:15.600
Science: C minus. Social Studies: D minus.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.600
Look at me when I'm talking, young man!

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:21.150
If these scores continue, I'll either have to...

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:24.190
...consult a counselor or call your mother in here.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.950
Now, which will it be? A counselor or your mother?

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:38.750
Hey, he's back! He's back! Hey, Al! You still alive?

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:43.090
What's eating you? What'd that hysterical old bat say?

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:47.010
Aw, man! She says she's gonna tell my mom about my grades.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:52.430
When Mom finds out, she's gonna ground me for a month!

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:56.770
Jeez, your mom's strict!

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:59.940
Oh, man, you can say that again.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:02.230
Hey, don't be so depressed.

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:03.820
You look depressed, Al.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:04.900
I do?

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:06.320
Were you picked on at school today?

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.530
No, not really.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:10.530
I guess it's okay, then.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:13.160
Test scores'll be coming out soon, right?

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.790
She must be psychic.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.470
Hold it!

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:11.340
I'm sorry, l...

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:14.100
What are you doing out this late?

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.890
I'm meeting my friends on a dare.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.600
Please don't tell my mom about this.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:23.440
Oh, a secret mission, huh?

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:24.520
Please!

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:25.900
I promise.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:30.650
Hey, can you take me with you next time?

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.330
Well, the truth is...

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:36.870
Keep this a secret, okay?

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:42.120
Girls aren't allowed to come. See you!

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:46.340
No girls allowed, huh?

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:21.040
Looks like they took away all the weapons.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:36.800
Wha?! Ow, damn! What the? Hey!

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.100
Hey, it still works.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.800
Hey, it's tight in there. Careful, now.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:22.680
What's that?

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.440
A body. Okay, we're done.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:31.190
Hi. Had some bad luck, too, huh?

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:39.410
What?

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.830
<i>Special forces vessel,</i> <i>clear for launch.</i>

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:46.330
Roger!

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:00.680
20 minutes to operation start.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.220
Beginning Minovsky particle broadcast.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:06.390
He's here. Send the special forces vessel out ahead of us.

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:10.480
<i>Special forces vessel, launch</i> <i>out and proceed towards Side 6.</i>

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:11.440
<i>Roger!</i>

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:36.010
5 minutes to operation start!

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.800
Launch mobile suit teams!

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.970
Launching mobile suit teams!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.770
There they go.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:55.610
It's started.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:03.160
Let's do it!

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:39.820
Just hold together, you pile of junk!

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:51.330
<i>Commercial transport</i> Aqua Verde, <i>requesting landing clearance!</i>

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.580
<i>Commercial transport</i> Aqua Verde, <i>requesting landing clearance!</i>

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.420
This is the commercial transport <i>Aqua Verde!</i> Please come in!

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:58.670
Clear me for landing!

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:04.470
It worked.

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:26.530
A battle. They're fighting outside of the colony.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:21:00.400
Oh, man. It's a real mess out there.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:04.200
They got my buddy. Sorry, could you get him out for me?

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:09.580
Passport and landing permit?

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:14.540
I wish the Riah government would keep on top of this sort of thing.

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:18.590
Mobile suits fighting inside the perimeter...

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:21.670
They're gonna wreck my business!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:23.340
Name and ID number?

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:30.100
Walter Peterson. ID number PG 40983726.

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:34.310
Flight manifest and invoice?

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:40.690
Hey, careful with him! He isn't a doll, you know!

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.980
Receiver's credentials?

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:46.110
That's all the papers I have.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:49.120
If you don't have it, we'll have to inspect your cargo.

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:50.160
But!

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:52.200
You carrying something you wouldn't want us to see?!

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:57.750
No, that's not it at all! Come on, it's just one form...

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:01.540
We're not doing this because we're bored! Get all your papers ready!

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:03.590
This is deck B-423. Inspection!

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:09.140
Great, it's on time. Start unloading her.

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:10.140
Yes, sir.

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:13.140
Hey, we have to inspect that! Don't touch it!

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:17.730
Uh, sorry about this, sir. I represent the receiver.

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:20.980
Here're the credentials.

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:23.610
The form looks all right...

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:28.280
...but it's supposed to be submitted by the sender!

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.160
Uh, that's some construction equipment in there.

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:33.700
We have to get it delivered by today...

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:36.040
...or else they're going to hit us with late charges.

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:38.750
If that happens, our company'll go bankrupt!

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:42.000
I'll never be able to face my client!

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:44.630
Please, we don't have the time.

00:22:44.710 --> 00:22:46.840
All right, all right!

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:50.680
You mean it? Oh, thank you, sir...

00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:53.640
We're busy with this battle and other ships are waiting.

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:56.180
Just have all your paperwork in order from now on.

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:58.440
I fell asleep!

00:22:58.480 --> 00:23:00.730
Mom's gonna flip if she finds out about this!

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:20.170
Holy...

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:22.540
You stupid kid! Are you trying to get yourself killed?!

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:26.360
They're back! The Zeon soldiers came back to this colony!

00:24:27.020 --> 00:24:29.320
They came back!

00:25:15.420 --> 00:25:21.200
<i>On that night I told them that lie...</i>

00:25:15.420 --> 00:25:21.200
<i>uso wo tsuita yoru ni wa</i>

00:25:21.790 --> 00:25:27.930
<i>...I couldn't sleep. That's how scared I was.</i>

00:25:21.790 --> 00:25:27.930
<i>nemurezu ni kowakatta</i>

00:25:28.260 --> 00:25:34.340
<i>But no matter how bad of a fight we would have...</i>

00:25:28.260 --> 00:25:34.340
<i>donna kenka wo shite mo</i>

00:25:34.640 --> 00:25:41.210
<i>...by the next day, it would be forgotten.</i>

00:25:34.640 --> 00:25:41.210
<i>tsugi no hi wa wasureteita</i>

00:25:43.510 --> 00:25:48.690
<i>The sky would be so blue...</i>

00:25:43.510 --> 00:25:48.690
<i>sora ga aoi koto</i>

00:25:49.950 --> 00:25:56.030
<i>...and that would make me so glad.</i>

00:25:49.950 --> 00:25:56.030
<i>sore ga ureshikute</i>

00:25:56.660 --> 00:26:02.540
<i>There would be times when I'd doubt others...</i>

00:25:56.660 --> 00:26:02.540
<i>itsuka hito wo utagai</i>

00:26:03.160 --> 00:26:09.480
<i>...and I'd know the loneliness of living.</i>

00:26:03.160 --> 00:26:09.480
<i>ikiru sabishisa shiru koto mo</i>

00:26:09.540 --> 00:26:15.540
<i>But that was something I didn't notice then.</i>

00:26:09.540 --> 00:26:15.540
<i>ki ga tsukazu ni subete wo</i>

00:26:15.940 --> 00:26:20.980
<i>Back when I believed in everything...</i>

00:26:15.940 --> 00:26:20.980
shinjiteta koro

00:26:45.200 --> 00:26:47.210
NEXT EPISODE

00:26:47.500 --> 00:26:49.920
I promise! I won't tell anyone!

00:26:52.880 --> 00:26:53.960
Are you nuts?

00:26:54.500 --> 00:26:56.760
It's not like I fight with a gun or anything.

00:27:10.230 --> 00:27:12.230
WAR IN THE POCKET

00:27:12.230 --> 00:27:15.190
Episode 3 And at the End of the Rainbow?
